course: dictionary
lesson: 2088
title: Using clues to find a meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A new word can often be understood from the words around it. Look for a clue in the same sentence: «A contagious (catching) face cancer has killed many devils.» The words in brackets tell you what contagious means here: catching, so it can spread.
explain: Contagious describes an illness, feeling or laugh that spreads from one person to another. A contagious disease, such as a cold, flu or chickenpox, passes on when you touch or stand close to someone who has it. «Her laugh is contagious» means her laugh makes other people laugh too.
explain: Test your guess by putting it in the sentence in place of the hard word. If «A catching face cancer has killed many devils» still makes sense, your guess is probably right. If you are still not sure, check a dictionary.
fact: Contagious means able to spread from one person to another.
fact: A contagious illness passes on when you touch or stand close to someone who has it.
fact: Contagious can also describe a feeling, laugh or yawn that spreads quickly through a group.
fact: Washing hands, covering coughs and staying home when ill help stop contagious diseases spreading.
fact: Words in brackets, like «(catching)», often give you a quick synonym to help you understand.
exercise: «A contagious (catching) face cancer has killed many devils.» What does contagious mean here? | Very beautiful | Quite old | *Able to spread from one animal to another | Hungry
exercise: «Her laugh is contagious.» What does this mean? | *Her laugh makes other people laugh too | Her laugh hurts her throat | Her laugh is very quiet
exercise: Mum says, «Stay home, your cold is contagious.» Why does she say this? | Because the cold makes you taller | Because the cold is very long | *Because the cold can spread to other people
test:
Which of these is a contagious disease? | A rainbow | *Chickenpox | A bicycle | Sunshine
Which action helps stop a contagious illness spreading? | Sharing a drink with a friend who is ill | Hugging everyone at the bus stop | *Covering your cough | Going to every party while you have a fever
exam:
Read «A contagious (catching) face cancer has killed many devils.» Which clue helps you find the meaning of contagious? | The word devils | The word face | *The word catching in brackets
